Subject: [PATCH] feat(plugins): add one-shot guarded ctx.dispose_path seam
 [daveey]

Add host-owned hermes_cli.path_disposal.dispose_path and the JSON-only
PluginContext.dispose_path(path: str, *, reason: str) -> dict entrypoint.
Check parent-resolved/final-component-unfollowed scope and write denial
before unlink/rmtree; report disposed, missing, refused or error and log
actor/reason/path/outcome. A refusal is final, with no deletion fallback.

Consumer: disk-cleanup, whose stage-3 migration remains exclusively owned
by t_5885a5694e360983 and https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/3366.
This own-PR-first seam changes no disk-cleanup or custody files and adds
no veto registry or plugin_api.json listing (ctx methods are reflected
into the existing plugin host's ctx_methods).

Proof:
- Canonical scripts/run_tests.sh: new disposal tests plus unchanged
  test_plugins_context.py, test_plugin_host.py, test_disk_cleanup_plugin.py,
  test_boundary_lint.py and test_docs_drift.py: 88 passed, 1 skipped.
- Guard-deleted RED: replace the scope refusal condition with False;
  test_outside, test_home_root, test_traversal,
  test_parent_symlink_traversal and test_tmp_root_and_child all fail (5).
- Guard-deleted RED: replace is_write_denied condition with False;
  test_write_denied fails (1). Restore both guards and canonical rerun
  passes, together with the mcp structured-content ctx consumer tests.
- Real unprivileged read-only parent returns error; real plugin host
  child round-trips disposed/missing dicts and plugin actor audit logs.
- scripts/hermes-python scripts/check --base origin/main: 21 checks pass.
- Boundary baseline and plugin_api.json unchanged. Docs include capability
  row, signature/outcomes/scope/no-fallback and disk-cleanup consumer.

